  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "\n\n\n\n\nProject Number: SCP-5000\r\n\r\nProject Class: Keter\r\n\r\nProject
    Title: Labyrinth of Infinity\r\n\r\nSpecial Containment Procedures: SCP-5000
    is contained within Site-\u03A9, a containment facility designed with infinite
    spatial characteristics. The interior of the facility is structured as an ever-changing
    labyrinth to ensure that SCP-5000 cannot be escaped from. Site-\u03A9 is equipped
    with advanced navigation systems and emergency response mechanisms to deal with
    anomalous activities within SCP-5000.\r\n\r\nDescription: SCP-5000 is an anomalous
    space that manifests as an infinitely expanding and ever-changing laboratory
    and park area. Once entered, all exits become indistinguishable, trapping anyone
    inside. The space contains multiple laboratories, each housing different SCP
    entities. Over time, these entities awaken and begin to roam the park.\r\n\r\nAnomalous
    Properties of SCP-5000:\r\n\r\nInfinite Expansion: The interior space of SCP-5000
    is infinitely large, with no discernible boundaries or exits.\r\nExtradimensional
    Breach: SCP-5000 appears to exist outside of regular space, not subject to the
    laws of physics.\r\nEntity Awakening: SCP entities contained within SCP-5000
    gradually awaken and become active, with diverse behavior patterns and abilities,
    increasing the difficulty of containment.\r\nShifting Labyrinth: The labyrinth
    structure within SCP-5000 constantly changes, making it difficult for anyone
    inside to find a fixed path.\r\nContainment Measures:\r\n\r\nRegular Patrols:
    Security personnel from Site-\u03A9 must regularly patrol the interior of SCP-5000
    to monitor the activities of SCP entities and prevent their escape.\r\nEntity
    Surveillance: All SCP entities contained within SCP-5000 are to be equipped with
    surveillance devices for real-time monitoring.\r\nEmergency Response: In the
    event of an SCP entity escaping its containment area, an emergency response team
    must be immediately deployed to re-contain the entity using appropriate means.\r\nResearch
    and Analysis: The research team at Site-\u03A9 must continuously study the characteristics
    of SCP-5000 to find potential breakthroughs in containment or methods of escape.\r\nAddendum:
    SCP-5000 was discovered accidentally during an exploration of an unknown anomalous
    space. Since its discovery, the SCP Foundation has been working to understand
    and control this phenomenon. Due to its infinite expansion, SCP-5000 is considered
    an extremely dangerous containment object, with any individual entering potentially
    facing life-threatening risks. Currently, the SCP Foundation is seeking ways
    to stabilize or close this anomalous space to prevent it from having a greater
    impact on the real world."
